Adds the website name to every store option of the DeepL translator in the admin panel.

Problem: the target-store split buttons (product, category, product attribute, CMS block, CMS page),
the mass-action store list with its source-store popup (product grid, CMS block and page grids),
the "Translate Source" attribute dropdown (product and category) and the source store in the module
configuration all label a store as "Store view name - locale". On a multi-website installation the
same store view name and locale are used on several websites (e.g. "Deutsch - de_DE" three times),
so the admin user has to guess which store a translation is read from or written to.

Fix: every label is built as "Website name / Store view name - locale", e.g. "Scandic-Fashion / Deutsch - de_DE".
Option values (store IDs) and request URLs are unchanged.

